From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:52:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: hotdog: enable Adreno 640 GPU

Enable the A640 GPU and GMU already described by the SM8150 base DTS, and
provide the handset-specific signed ZAP firmware path.

This was validated on an HD1913 with the upstream msm DRM driver, Turnip,
and two headless Vulkan workloads. The GMU loads firmware v2.0.261 and the
GPU exposes all six expected OPPs without IOMMU faults or recovery events.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts   | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -231,6 +231,18 @@
 	reg = <0x0 0x99515000 0x0 0x2000>;
 };
 
+&gmu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&gpu {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	zap-shader {
+		firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/oneplus/hotdog/a640_zap.mbn";
+	};
+};
+
 &spss_mem {
 	reg = <0x0 0x99600000 0x0 0x100000>;
 };
-- 
2.50.1
